# expected.list — parity classifications for the Gleam corpus runner (feature 050).
# Read by run_gleam_corpus.sh. Entries are VERIFIED classifications (Bug Protocol), not
# pre-judgements: a case is added here only after its divergence is actually observed and
# root-caused. Grammar (first token):
#   blocked <block> <reason>  Gleam cannot RUN this case (engine limitation). Excluded from
#                             the agreement denominator, but SURFACED in the report.
#   gap <block> <reason>      Verified semantic GAP (out-of-MVP predicate/feature). Expected
#                             divergence: compared + surfaced, not counted against SC-001.
#   fork <block> <reason>     Owner-gated FORK (e.g. FORK-1). Recorded, never forced to agree.
#
# T039 seeded verified-blocked blocks (since fixed & removed at T042). GAP/FORK rows
# are added as divergences are observed + classified.


